-A new, independent C++20 implementation. **M0/M1 are complete for their documented Linux scope; M2 is in progress.** The app now mounts REZ archives, reads DAT v56 geometry and typed properties, and runs a supported subset of original objects in an in-game inspector. ABC skeletal/vertex animation, model callbacks and primary-world collision are implemented. Selected original shell/CPlayerObj entry, inventory, Beretta/knife animation and vector-fire/damage branches and original MoveMgr dry-land movement, stairs, crouch and body locomotion animations, containers, liquids, ladders, conveyors and damage/freefall volumes, original sliding doors and translating world-model collision are connected; complete player gameplay remains missing. This is not a playable game.
